    <string name="onboarding_log_eyebrow">LOG</string>
    <string name="onboarding_log_title">Log the dose when you take it</string>
    <string name="onboarding_log_body">PillMate is for as-needed medication: the kind you take when you need it. There are no schedules to keep and no alarms chasing you.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_log_note">One tap is enough. Also from the widget and from the notification, without opening the app.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_clock_eyebrow">THE CLOCK</string>
    <string name="onboarding_clock_title">Your day on a 24-hour clock</string>
    <string name="onboarding_clock_body">Each dot is a dose, placed at its time and in the colour of its medication. 00 is at the top and it turns like a normal clock.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_clock_note">Try it: tap a dot to see what it was.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_rhythm_eyebrow">YOUR RHYTHM</string>
    <string name="onboarding_rhythm_title">With more days, your pattern shows up</string>
    <string name="onboarding_rhythm_body">Put several days together and the dots turn into bars: the longer the bar, the more doses at that hour. PillMate works out your most active hour and how often you usually take a dose.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_rhythm_note">It describes, it doesn\'t judge: no scores, no goals and no medical advice.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_privacy_eyebrow">PRIVACY</string>
    <string name="onboarding_privacy_title">What you log never leaves your phone</string>
    <string name="onboarding_privacy_body">No accounts, no ads and no analytics. Your data is yours and stays with you.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_tap_hint">Tap the tile</string>
    <plurals name="onboarding_today_doses">
        <item quantity="one">Today: %1$d dose</item>
